start language dictionary

type:action

*-> action      - action: action="desc" declares any function - standalone abstract or entity function (two canonical forms)
    -> exm: abstract "open_file" -> action="open file by name"   // declares function: open_file
    -> exm: open_file("main.txt")                             // usage
    -> exm: file:action="grant access to user":name="access"    // declares entity function: file:access
    -> exm: file:access(context:user)                         // usage
    -> exm: action==run

*-> add          - logical adding entity action 
    -> exm: xml files add to prj

*-> anchor       - forced anchor: an explicit action-level anchor, the node is pinned by hand; this is the compiled glyph form of the textual operator &->

*-> answer - answer to user.
    -> exm:answ:->;usr
    -> exm:answ:lng=usr:lang

*-> approve - approve
    -> exm:apr:true

*-> ask          - request; RESOLUTION ORDER: first ask the base (dictionary/syntax/protos/blueprints via RAG search/get) - if the answer is already recorded, do NOT ask again; only if the base has no answer, ask the human; never guess or invent - this frees the human from repeated questions; the constructor is a contract between human and AI, and a human can programme in this language too
    -> exm:ask:->prompt

*-> async         - action async run of any entity

*-> balance, pan - action of precise correction of imprecise entities  
    -> exm: llm:creative:factor[0,100]:pan(20)

*-> build         - build/assembly of any entity

*-> call         - entry / function call
    -> exm: call:fn()

*-> change - change
    -> exm:change:->file:name

*-> close        - generic canonical act function on any entity: close(<entity>) - finalizes the entity and saves its bound node state, declared once via act, works for every entity
    -> exm: close(file name="out.xml")

*-> codrev           - code anallize, review without editing, testing
    -> exm:codrev:->source

*-> compil        - compilation, compile
    -> exm:compil:->code

*-> compress      - compress action of any entity
    -> exm: compress(llm:token)

*-> create - action create: create a file, api, class, function etc. (create action; pairs with its target: crt fun, crt file, crt api)
    -> exm:create:fun:name="load"
    -> exm:create [code, data, file]
    -> exm:create:fun:name="load"

*-> delay   - delay or period
    -> exm:delay(500) - delay 500 times
    -> exm:delay:2s   - delay 2 seconds
    -> exm:delay()    - infinite delay

*-> delete, remove - remove
    -> exm:rm:->file:name="main"

*-> deploy           - code compilation or deployment
    -> exm:deploy:->action="deploy to server"

*-> exam, scan - scaning, examination
    -> exm:scan:->file

*-> exec, run - execute, run, sequence, request action in program, not you
    -> exm:run:->exec

*-> extract      - extract action
    -> exm:fun create (file name="out.xml" alias xml ): -> open(file name="project.exe"):alias source:->extract(source *? data:type=dom to xml)

*-> function - function: an action when it is a rule or an agent; an API entry point when it is a spec or architecture; often used with the par key (parameter) and ret (return), the logic is preferably written through the language logical operators
    -> exm:fun:type=rule:scop=root
    -> exm:fun:name="load":par="val1"
    -> exm:func:name="load"
    -> exm:function:name="load"
    -> exm:create:fun:name="load":par="val1"
    -> exm:create:fun:type="web api": par "in":type="text":desc="vibedsl request" :-> srch(in) type="RAG":-> return

*-> get          - action to obtain any entity 
    -> exm: get:data:source

*-> insert      - logical action insert of any entity
    -> exm:insrt:row
    -> exm:if(dir:empty):insert(file)

*-> load         - load action: load a view, file or base by name
    -> exm:load(view name="main")
    -> exm:event:onCreate -> load(view name="main")

*-> make - make
    -> exm:mk:->file

*-> modify       - logic modify: modify/alter the logic (not a class/module - those are module/class)
    -> exm:mod specfile:logic=specfile:logic+rule

*-> move         - logical move action
    -> exm:db1:move(table)->db2

*-> only         - only, verifiication action
    -> exm:only:check

*-> open         - generic canonical act function on any entity: open(<entity>) - opens the entity bound node for changes, declared once via act, works for every entity
    -> exm: open(file name="out.xml")
    -> exm: open(user name="alice")

*-> plan         - make plan mode or cpecs
    -> exm:plan:->specs

*-> rebuild          - action rebuild any entity
    -> exm:event(exam(obj):type==exm)<>:
            ->rebuild()
            ->show()

*-> remake          - logical remake

*-> remember      - implicit anchor: id definition, plain remember command

*-> replaced        - logical replaced of any entity
    -> exm:dpd:old

*-> request - action request from llm to user
    -> exm:request:post

*-> retry        - action retry
    -> exm:retry(5)

*-> return - return any object action
    -> exm:return:val
    -> exm:return:val

*-> revert, rollb - revert, return previos state, rollback
    -> exm:rollb:state

*-> review      - review
    -> exm:rvw:->;code

*-> save         - generic canonical act function on any entity: save(<entity>) - persists the entity to its bound node, declared once via act, works for every entity
    -> exm: save(file name="out.xml")
            prj "site" Etalon("www.other-site.com")
            prj "service"  Etalon("BranchCache"):OS="Windows"

*-> scrsht         - screenshot
    -> exm:scrsht:path

*-> select       - select action, syntax example sel[val1,val2] after ->swt if more way or ->abstract{} if abstract, example sel[val1,val2]->fun data=sel:ret , sel[val1,val2]->swt case val1: data1=val1 bk
    -> exm:sel[v1,v2]->switch
    -> exm:fun par:name="a":type="list" -> list:sel[n]:fun ->(item:date > item:date)->return

*-> set          - setter action of any entity
    -> exm: table:xml event:onOpen->set(data)

*-> show         - action show any entity in user out default text console 
    -> exm: show(dict)

*-> split     - split anything into n parts by vectors, e.g. split a dictionary into its category parts and save
    -> exm: split(dict,[actions,mapping,operators,abstracts])<>:
            -> save(dict:"action")
            -> save(dict:"mapping")
            -> save(dict:"operators")
            -> save(dict:"abstracts")

*-> srch         - search action: search over a node/base by query
    -> exm:srch(in) type="RAG"

*-> store           - logic store of any entity

*-> tick         - time elapse, example [llm:con:out:txt="hi im here" tic(1m)], print message to user "im here" after 1m
    -> exm:tic(1m)

*-> trim         - action: trim/strip characters from a string or collection (default whitespace)
    -> exm:name=trim("  hello  ")

*-> use          - logical import command: apply/engage an object, prototype or import; the logical side of import (import is the physical lib/item, use is the logical command that engages it)
    -> exm:use(agent name="dsl-coder")
    -> exm:use(VibeDSL:proto[if,goal,fail])

*-> variant - action reduce variants
    -> exm: fun:type=rule -> if(event(?))-> show(?:variant(5))
    -> exm: fun:type=rule -> if(event(?))-> show(?:variant(5 with ask))

*-> write - write action
    -> exm:write:goal
